"The postoperative pathology reveals a Gleason 4+3 (ISUP grade group 3) and pathological stage pT3a. Adverse findings include positive surgical margins, as noted by the surgical pathology report stating, \"surgical margins were positive.\" Conversely, the seminal vesicles were not invaded, and lymphovascular invasion was absent. Nodal status is documented as \"no lymph nodes were removed,\" which means the pNx status does not establish node-negative disease. The preoperative PSA is not recorded, and consequently, the postoperative PSA and its trajectory remain unknown, which significantly widens the uncertainty regarding biochemical recurrence. The documented positive margins represent a significant adverse factor. The absence of documented nodal sampling limits staging and does not establish node-negative disease. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory is crucial for revising the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 41.09 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 24.66–57.53 months; its coverage has not been validated."
